Apply workspace changes back to the base directory

Usage: forkspace merge [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>  Name of the workspace to merge

Options:
      --commit             Create a git commit with the merged changes
  -m, --message <MESSAGE>  Commit message (implies --commit)
      --patch              Generate a unified patch instead of merging
      --drop               Drop the workspace after a successful merge
      --no-install         Skip automatic dependency installation after merge
      --dry-run            Show the merge plan without applying it
      --resume             Resume an interrupted merge
      --overwrite-base     Overwrite conflicting changes in the base
      --quiet              Suppress the pre-apply plan summary
  -h, --help               Print help
